 "finding": "Scenes generated through the forward model (the lab's solver for each cavity's imprint, the synthesizer for the image), with the unrelated ground and shaking matched. At the strongest amplified diagnostic (each imprint boosted to 2 rad) the reference detector told the shaking names the layout in 78% of images (chance 33%) and places it 33.9 m from where it lies (median; the controls' peaks lie 36.5 m away); the published method's plan map read blind names it in 33% and places it 3.1 m away, and its change against the same ground without the cavity (a diagnostic it never has) 67% and 2.5 m (the controls' top places lie a median 3.4 m from the footprints). At the real level the reference detector names 33% and the published blind map 33%. The reference detector recovers the imposed layouts at the diagnostic, so the experiment can reveal a real signal. Amplified levels are diagnostics, not physical predictions."
}